ADR refs      : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015

Architecture  : stateless @Composable screen (AlertsListPage / AlertsListPageContent) driven by a
                Hilt-free AndroidX ViewModel (AlertsListPageViewModel : BaseFeedViewModel) that binds
                the shared KMP core (ADR-004) via the AlertsListPageSource seam:
                  useAlerts             -> NotificationsRepository.alerts()        (cache-then-network Resource)
                  useAlertRules         -> NotificationsRepository.alertRules()     (cache-then-network Resource)
                  useAlertDetail        -> NotificationsRepository.alertDetail(id)  (cache-then-network Resource)
                  usePinned('alert_rule')-> PinnedRepository.pinned(AlertRule)      (pinned-first ordering)
                  useMarkAlertRead      -> NotificationsRepository.markAlertRead    (POST /alerts/{id}/read)
                  useAcknowledgeAlert   -> NotificationsRepository.acknowledgeAlert (POST /alerts/{id}/ack)
                  useReopenAlert        -> NotificationsRepository.reopenAlert      (POST /alerts/{id}/reopen)
                The host builds page-local HttpNotificationsRepository + HttpPinnedRepository over the
                SAME shared resilient ApiHttpClient + offline CacheStore the other repositories use
                (the DataContainer wires no NotificationsStore yet — identical to the sibling DrivesList
                / Statistics surfaces' page-local reads), so the ADR-013 freshness contract +
                SI-verbatim caching are preserved with NO DataContainer change. Every panel is a
                Material 3 Surface/Card (GlassPanel / KpiOverviewCard / MetricCard); both charts use the
                A3 native chart layer (BarChartWrapper for the 7-day trend, a Compose-canvas donut +
                legend for the by-type pie — never a webview); every string resolves from res/values via
                stringResource (ADR-014); the success toasts ride a Material 3 SnackbarHost; the
                quiet-hours window reuses the A6 QuietHours value at the display boundary. No field in
                this domain is unit-bearing, so there is no SI conversion — only locale/timezone
                formatting at the render boundary.

